But, again, that is my interpretation of it.

01:16:05.000 --> 01:16:10.000
Well, here comes the point.

01:16:10.000 --> 01:16:15.000
My manners believe, and I make it in my third part when we talk about cosmology,

01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:25.000
that Aristotle was the first person that articulated, formulated the laws of reason.

01:16:25.000 --> 01:16:32.000
For my manners, the most important work of Aristotle are not his metaphysics or his physics,

01:16:32.000 --> 01:16:36.000
but rather the organon, the books on logic.

01:16:36.000 --> 01:16:37.000
Yes?

01:16:37.000 --> 01:16:43.000
So, therefore, he believed that my manners, and I'm sorry, that Aristotle represents

01:16:43.000 --> 01:16:50.000
the emergence of pagan humanity from mythical thought into rationality.

01:16:50.000 --> 01:17:00.000
Now, however, in this book, I show that one of the points that my manners try to show

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:07.000
is that there is a world beyond rationality.

01:17:07.000 --> 01:17:16.000
That at certain points, rationality is wanting.

01:17:16.000 --> 01:17:22.000
And then, that is the moment of crisis.

01:17:22.000 --> 01:17:26.000
In Arabic, you are hayran, perplexed.

01:17:26.000 --> 01:17:31.000
